THIRD-PARTY REFERENCE MATERIAL

Two tables in this codebase were cross-checked against outside sources rather than derived
solely from the disks. They are attributed here so the provenance is not lost:

  * backend/wl_item.py — the item TYPE and CLASS enumerations follow the analysis published in
    wastelib by Klaus Reimer (https://github.com/kayahr/wastelib). Structural facts about the
    file format, arrived at independently but confirmed against that work.

  * backend/wl_cell.py — the weapon statistics table was cross-checked against the
    "Nearly Ultimate Wasteland Guide", a fan-maintained document. The numbers are balance data
    read out of the game; the guide served as a second opinion, not as the source.

If either table is ever expanded by copying from those sources rather than from the game's own
bytes, the licensing of that source needs to be settled first.


REVERSE ENGINEERING

The formats here were reverse-engineered from a legally owned copy for the purpose of
interoperability — reading and writing the game's own data files. That is the entire scope of
this project.
